# Tauri / Rust (desktop / OS separation)

## Local and OS-specific behavior

When implementing **behavior tied to local disk or the desktop environment** (file paths, shell integration, OS APIs, platform-specific behavior, etc.), follow these rules.

1. **Access only through a trait (or equivalent abstraction)** — callers must not depend directly on a concrete OS implementation.
2. **Keep per-OS / per-environment code in trait implementations** — e.g. `#[cfg(target_os = "windows")]` stays in implementation modules; commands and app layers see only the abstraction.
3. **Tests and future swaps** — structure mocks and stubs behind the same trait.

When adding new commands or services, if platform branches start spreading inside command functions, refactor toward a trait split with separate implementations.
